    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="1026" n="930" xml:id="pg930"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760g.61/62: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-08T17:00:00+03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:04 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>129. A Moscow radio dated April 6th announces the occupation of Erivan by the
                    Soviet forces. This apparently means the overthrow of the Vratzian
                    anti-Bolshevik Government in Armenia which had regained Erivan at the time of
                    the Bolshevik attack on Georgia. See my 64, February 24 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >21</hi>].<anchor n="48" xml:id="d887-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
